In chapter "4.5 Line numbers" is a wrong example output:

````md
```{r, attr.source='.numberLines'}`r ''`
if (TRUE) {
  1:10
}
```
````

The output is:

```{r, attr.source='.numberLines', eval=FALSE}
if (TRUE) {
  x <- 1:10
  x + 1
}
```

This is obviously wrong. I created a pull request to correct the example.

colorize = function(x, color){
  if (knitr::is_latex_output()) {
    sprintf("\\textcolor{%s}(%s)", color, x)
  } else if (knitr::is_html_output()) {
    sprintf("<font color='%s'>%s</font>", color, x)
  } else x
}

should be brackets not parantheses for the latex output

colorize = function(x, color){
  if (knitr::is_latex_output()) {
    sprintf("\\textcolor{%s}{%s}", color, x)
  } else if (knitr::is_html_output()) {
    sprintf("<font color='%s'>%s</font>", color, x)
  } else x
}

