Follow the example of about a chunk hook `wrapper = TRUE`
https://github.com/yihui/knitr-examples/blob/master/062-chunk-wrapper.Rmd

````
```{r setup}
library(knitr)
knit_hooks$set(wrapper = function(before, options, envir) {
  if (before) {
    sprintf('    ```{r %s}\n', options$params.src)
  } else '    ```\n'
})
```
```` 
One of the trick is that every options of the chunk is in `options$param.src`.

It will output as is, including the chunk backticks part
````

```{r test_label, wrapper=TRUE, eval=FALSE}
1+1
plot(1)
```
